@startuml
title Helper amortisation — m linear MSMs collapse into one opening argument
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  ParticipantBorderColor #7A5BB5
  ArrowColor #7A5BB5
  LifeLineBorderColor #7A5BB5
  NoteBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  NoteBorderColor #7A5BB5
}

participant "m proofs" as PR
participant "Untrusted helper" as H
participant "Verifier V" as V

PR -> H : challenges (u_1, ..., u_k) from each of the m proofs
note right of H
  each proof would otherwise cost V
  one O(d) multi-scalar multiplication
end note

H -> V : the group elements G_1, ..., G_m
H -> V : opening argument for a random linear\ncombination of the m commitments

note right of V
  V computes the claimed opening value itself
  in O(m log d), using the product form
  g(X, u) = prod_i (u_i + u_i^{-1} X^{2^{i-1}})
end note

V -> V : check ONE polynomial commitment opening
note over V #F3EEFB
  amortised cost per proof: O(log d)
  instead of O(d)
  the helper is untrusted: a wrong G_i
  makes the opening argument fail
end note
@enduml
